    "about": "Badri Narayanan temple (Tamil: பத்ரி நாராயணன் கோயில்) is a Hindu temple in the Madurai District in the entrance of Alagar Koil in the state of Tamil Nadu, India. The temple is built in the style of the Badrinath temple, Uttarakhand. Balaji is in a seated position in this temple. An idol of Adi Shankaracharya — an important Hindu saint in 8th century AD — is placed alongside of the temple."
